<title>ITALY: Gross yields fall at Italian BTP bond auction.</title>
<headline>Gross yields fall at Italian BTP bond auction.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Auction results for a first tranche of 3.0 trillion lire worth of three-year Italian Treasury fixed rate bonds (BTPs) with a 6.00 percent coupon, and a eleventh tranche of 2.0 trillion lire of five-year BTPs carrying a 6.25 percent coupon.</p>
<p>		  May 15, 2000   pvs	March 1, 2002   pvs</p>
<p> Net Yield	 5.45 pct    5.89	  5.71 pct     6.16</p>
<p> Gross Yield     6.24 pct    6.67	  6.56 pct     7.02</p>
<p> Assigned price 99.60	 98.55	 97.35	  97.35</p>
<p> Bids	     6.822 trln lire	   6.147 trln lire</p>
<p> Assigned	 3.000 trln lire	   2.000 trln lire</p>
<p>Note - Comparisons are given with a previous auction on April 30. The three-year BTP is against a previous eleventh tranche of Feb 15 2000 paper and is therefore not directly compariable.</p>
</text>
